---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/consts';
import { useLocale } from '~/i18n/routing';

const locale = useLocale(Astro.currentLocale, Astro.url.pathname);
const title = locale === 'zh' ? '关于' : 'About';
const description = locale === 'zh'
  ? '关于站点与作者。'
  : 'About the journal and its author.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="container about-hero">
    {locale === 'zh' ? (
      <>
        <div class="about-hero__kicker">关于 · 作者</div>
        <h1 class="about-hero__name">{SITE.author}</h1>
        <p class="about-hero__role">
          做高速数字、信号完整性、硅光，以及把一套 EDA 流程拴在一起的那点 Python。
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <div class="about-hero__kicker">About · The Author</div>
        <h1 class="about-hero__name">{SITE.author}</h1>
        <p class="about-hero__role">
          Engineer working on high-speed digital, signal integrity, silicon
          photonics, and the small Python that holds an EDA workflow together.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="prose-container">
    <div class="prose">
      {locale === 'zh' ? (
        <>
          <h2>这个站是什么</h2>
          <p>
            <em>The Fierceman Journal</em> 是一份个人技术笔记，主要记录我在
            ADS、SIPro、EMPro 以及与之相关的 Python 自动化工作中遇到的细节、
            踩过的坑，和那些"看起来理所当然但跑起来不对"的经验。
          </p>
          <p>
            内容覆盖：信号完整性 (SI) 与电源完整性 (PI)、系统级光电链路、
            硅光器件、EM 求解器的工程化使用、ADS 自动化 API（含 EMPro / RFPro / SIPro）、
            以及偶尔的工具开发与 MCP server 实验。
          </p>
          <p>
            硅光这一支记的是器件。条形波导、耦合器，用 Lumerical MODE 的 FDE 来算，
            读书路径跟着 Chrostowski 与 Hochberg 的
            <em>Silicon Photonics Design</em>。
            器件归 SiPh；MZM、TIA 和链路 budget 仍归 EOE。
          </p>

          <h2>为什么叫 Journal</h2>
          <p>
            不是教程，是工程日志，也不追新闻。
            节奏不快，但每一篇都写到我自己满意为止。
            如果哪一篇让你少踩一个坑，就达到了它存在的目的。
          </p>

          <h2>联系</h2>
          <p>
            每篇文章底部都有一个留言框，不用注册任何账号，写个昵称就能发。
            也可以直接邮件联系：<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>。
          </p>
          <p>
            如果你在做 ADS / EMPro 自动化，或者在折腾 SIPro 的奇怪行为，
            欢迎聊聊。硅光器件（MODE / FDE）上的具体问题，同样欢迎。
          </p>

          <h2>后记</h2>
          <p>
            标题与正文用 <strong>Fraunces</strong>，元信息用
            <strong>Inter</strong>，代码用
            <strong>JetBrains Mono</strong>。用
            <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>
            搭建，经 GitHub Pages 部署。强调色是一种深波尔多红
            （<code style="color: var(--accent);">#7a1631</code>），用得很省。
          </p>
          <p>
            文字与原创图示为
            <a href="/LICENSE">All Rights Reserved</a>。
            未经书面许可不得转载或演绎；短引用请署名，并链接原文。
            站点源码公开，只为把这份日志部署出去，并不授权再利用其中的内容。
            文中代码片段除非另有说明，仍以 MIT 提供。
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <h2>What this site is</h2>
          <p>
            <em>The Fierceman Journal</em> is a personal engineering notebook.
            It keeps the details I run into while working in ADS, SIPro, EMPro,
            and the Python that automates them — the pits, and the things that
            look obvious until they refuse to run.
          </p>
          <p>
            The ground it covers: signal integrity and power integrity,
            system-level electro-optical links, silicon photonic devices,
            the engineering use of EM solvers, the ADS automation APIs
            (EMPro, RFPro, SIPro), and the occasional tool or MCP server experiment.
          </p>
          <p>
            The silicon-photonics line is about devices. Strip waveguides and
            couplers, solved with the FDE solver in Lumerical MODE, read along
            Chrostowski and Hochberg's <em>Silicon Photonics Design</em>.
            Devices belong to SiPh. An MZM, a TIA, and a link budget still belong to EOE.
          </p>

          <h2>Why "Journal"</h2>
          <p>
            Not a tutorial, and not a news feed. An engineering log.
            The pace is slow, and a piece goes up only when I am satisfied with it.
            If one of them saves you a pit, it has done what it is here for.
          </p>

          <h2>Get in touch</h2>
          <p>
            Every essay ends with a note box. No account — a name is enough.
            Or write directly: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are automating ADS or EMPro, or chasing some strange SIPro
            behavior, I would like to hear it. Concrete questions on silicon
            photonic devices (MODE / FDE) are welcome too.
          </p>

          <h2>Colophon</h2>
          <p>
            Typeset in <strong>Fraunces</strong> (serif headlines and body) and
            <strong>Inter</strong> (sans-serif metadata), with code in
            <strong>JetBrains Mono</strong>. Built with
            <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>
            and deployed via GitHub Pages. The accent is a deep Bordeaux
            (<code style="color: var(--accent);">#7a1631</code>), used sparingly.
          </p>
          <p>
            The writing and the original figures are
            <a href="/LICENSE">All Rights Reserved</a>.
            They may not be republished or adapted without written permission.
            A short quotation should carry a name and a link to the original.
            The site source is public so this journal can be deployed; that does
            not license the contents for reuse. Code fragments in the essays
            remain MIT unless a note says otherwise.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
